{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% set h = q1.home %}
{% block title %}Czech hockey · Player pool atlas{% endblock %}
{% block description %}The Czech professional hockey player pool measured against nine peer nations: NHL and top European league players per million inhabitants, when the NHL group fell, where the cohorts are thin, ice time for the young at home, how Czech players fare abroad, what the national team is built from. Public data, reproducible.{% endblock %}
{% block canonical %}https://hockey.bsandova.com/{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}<script defer src="charts.js?v={{ v }}"></script>{% endblock %}

{% macro nation_table(rows, key_n, key_pm, noun) %}
<table class="fig-table">
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Nation</th><th scope="col" class="num">{{ noun }}</th><th scope="col" class="num">per million</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for n in rows|sort(attribute=key_pm, reverse=True) %}
    <tr{% if n.iso3 == 'CZE' %} class="is-home"{% endif %}><td>{{ n.name }}</td><td class="num">{{ n[key_n] }}</td><td class="num">{{ f2(n[key_pm]) }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endmacro %}

{% block body %}
<a class="skip-link" href="#take">Skip to content</a>

<header class="report-header">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Czech hockey: <em>the player pool</em></h1>
    <p class="masthead-subtitle">How deep is the Czech professional pool, measured against nine peer nations · {{ q1.season }}</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="hero" id="summary">
  <img class="hero-photo" src="img/hockey.jpg" srcset="img/hockey-1200.jpg 1200w, img/hockey.jpg 1920w" sizes="100vw" alt="A hockey player carrying the puck across the ice, in black and white with only the blue of his jersey kept" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-num">
        <span class="hero-num-figure">{{ f2(h.nhl_per_million) }}<span class="ast" aria-hidden="true">*</span></span>
        <span class="hero-num-unit">Czech NHL players per million inhabitants, {{ q1.season }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-lead">
        <p class="hero-finding">
          Per head, Czechia ranks {{ ordinal(h.rank_nhl) }} of {{ q1.n_nations }} nations in the NHL and {{ ordinal(h.rank_top5) }} in the NHL plus the four strongest European leagues.
          The Czech NHL group peaked at {{ q1.peak.n }} players in {{ q1.peak.season }}; it is {{ q1.peak.latest.n }} now.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-path">Three minutes: this number and the six findings below. The rest is the evidence.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-footnote">* {{ h.nhl }} Czech players with at least 20 of 82 NHL games (pro-rated to the schedule) in {{ q1.season }}, per {{ f1(population_m) }} million inhabitants (Eurostat); every peer counted the same way. <a href="#methodology">Methodology</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="hero-credit">Photo: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jake_Levin_(Air_Force_Falcon%27s_men%27s_ice_hockey)_during_game_against_Bentley_Falcons_men%27s_ice_hockey_at_Cadet_Arena_in_Colorado_Springs_on_November_9,_2018_(45170233234).jpg">U.S. Air Force Academy</a> · public domain, colour held</p>
</section>

<section class="take" id="take">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="close-kicker">What to take from it</p>
    {% for t in take %}
    <div class="nx-take"><p class="nx-take-n">{{ loop.index }}</p><div><p class="nx-take-head">{{ t.head }}</p>{% for b in t.body %}<p class="nx-take-body">{{ b }}</p>{% endfor %}</div></div>
    {% endfor %}
    <p class="take-line close-links"><a href="#scope">What is counted</a> · <a href="#limitations">Limitations</a> · {% if autumn %}<a href="#autumn">This autumn</a> · {% endif %}<a href="atlas/">Every Czech player in the pool</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide scope" id="scope">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="slide-q">What is counted</h2>
    <p class="slide-a">Ten nations, six leagues, one definition of nationality, and three leagues and one database left out on purpose.</p>
    <div class="scope-grid">
      <div>
        <h3>The ladder</h3>
        <dl class="scope-list">
          <dt><i class="sw" style="background:var(--acid)"></i>Rung 1</dt><dd>NHL.</dd>
          <dt><i class="sw" style="background:#111111"></i>Rung 2</dt><dd>SHL (Sweden), Liiga (Finland), National League (Switzerland), DEL (Germany). "NHL + rung 2" is the headline's five leagues.</dd>
          <dt><i class="sw" style="background:#c9c9c4"></i>Home</dt><dd>The Czech Extraliga. For Finland, Sweden, Switzerland and Germany the home league is already rung 2.</dd>
          <dt><i class="sw" style="background:#8a8a8a"></i>Other</dt><dd>Everything else in the data.</dd>
        </dl>
        <p class="scope-note">Nations: Czechia against {{ peers|join(', ') }}. Population: Eurostat, 1 January of the season's second year.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 id="nationality">Nationality, one definition</h3>
        <p>A player's nationality is taken, in this order, from:</p>
        <ol class="scope-ol">
          <li><strong>citizenship</strong> where a league publishes it: the NHL's <code>nationalityCode</code>, the Liiga's and the SHL's <code>nationality</code> (the SHL's is mostly "N/A" before about 2010);</li>
          <li>the <strong>national-team roster</strong> at a World Championship or Olympics since 2010 (IIHF eligibility);</li>
          <li><strong>eligibility or licence</strong> where that is all a source has: the Extraliga's foreigner flag, the DEL's licence nationality (from 2022/23), the National League's Swiss licence.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Players are linked across leagues on the folded name plus the birth date, so a Czech in the SHL is recognised from his NHL or Extraliga record. Czechoslovak-era births take the present-day state the NHL recodes them to. Of the {{ pool.players }} players on the <a href="atlas/">pool page</a>, {{ pool.eligibility_only }} are Czech on eligibility alone.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 id="exclusions">Left out</h3>
        <ul class="scope-ul">
          <li><strong>KHL</strong>, by design. It removes a real destination, especially before 2014, and it is where {{ pct0(q6.home.khl) }} of the Czech national team's roster spots since 2010 came from.</li>
          <li><strong>AHL</strong>: its terms forbid automated access. AHL seasons appear only in NHL players' career records, a survivor-biased view.</li>
          <li><strong>Slovak Extraliga</strong>: its robots.txt blocks automated access. Slovakia is measured through its players in the covered leagues.</li>
          <li><strong>Elite Prospects</strong>: its terms forbid scraping.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" id="q1">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="close-kicker">Question 1</p>
    <h2 class="slide-q">Is the Czech pool thin?</h2>
    <p class="slide-a">Not per head. Czechia ranks <strong>{{ ordinal(h.rank_nhl) }} of {{ q1.n_nations }}</strong> for NHL players at {{ f2(h.nhl_per_million) }} per million, {{ q1.nhl_vs_median_word }} the peer median of {{ f2(q1.peer_median.nhl_per_million) }}; {{ q1.top_nhl.name }} leads at {{ f2(q1.top_nhl.nhl_per_million) }}.</p>
    <figure class="figure-bleed" data-chart="q1-bars">
      {{ nation_table(q1.table, 'nhl', 'nhl_per_million', 'NHL players') }}
      <figcaption>How to read it: one bar per nation, players with at least the games threshold in {{ q1.season }} divided by the population in millions; the dashed line is the median of the nine peers. Switch to "NHL + rung 2" to add the SHL, Liiga, National League and DEL: Czechia has {{ h.top5 }} players there, {{ f2(h.top5_per_million) }} per million, {{ ordinal(h.rank_top5) }} of {{ q1.n_nations }} (peer median {{ f2(q1.peer_median.top5_per_million) }}).</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="figure-bleed" data-chart="q1-series">
      <table class="fig-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Season</th><th scope="col" class="num">Czech NHL players</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for r in q1.home_series %}<tr><td>{{ r.season }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.n if r.n is not none else 'lockout' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table>
      <figcaption>How to read it: each line is a nation's count per million, season by season; Czechia is the blue line, the two peers picked in the chips are ink and grey. The NHL series starts in {{ q1.first_season }} with {{ q1.first_n }} Czech players, rises to {{ q1.peak.n }} in {{ q1.peak.season }} and falls to {{ q1.peak.latest.n }} in {{ q1.peak.latest.season }}; 2004/05 was not played. The rung 1 + 2 series starts in {{ q1.top5_first_season }}; seasons before {{ q1.complete_first }} are shaded because the DEL did not publish nationality, so they are lower bounds.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <details class="fold slide-method">
      <summary>How we know</summary>
      <p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">What we did</span> For each nation and season we counted the distinct players of that nationality who reached the games threshold in the NHL (or in any of the five leagues), then divided by the population. The threshold is {{ q1.threshold_def }}: 20 games in a full NHL season, fewer in the short 2012/13 and 2020/21 seasons and in shorter European schedules.</p>
      <p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">Sensitivity</span> Counting any game at all, Czechia has {{ q1.sens_any.nhl }} NHL players ({{ f2(q1.sens_any.nhl_per_million) }} per million, {{ ordinal(q1.sens_any.rank_nhl) }}) and {{ q1.sens_any.top5 }} in the five leagues ({{ ordinal(q1.sens_any.rank_top5) }}). With a flat 20 games everywhere, {{ q1.sens_fixed.nhl }} and {{ q1.sens_fixed.top5 }} ({{ ordinal(q1.sens_fixed.rank_top5) }}).</p>
      <p class="slide-how"><span class="slide-how-label">Coverage</span> In {{ q1.season }} every qualifying NHL, Liiga and DEL player has a nationality; the National League has {{ q1.coverage.NL.unidentified }} of {{ q1.coverage.NL.qualifying }} unidentified (foreign licences with no match), the SHL {{ q1.coverage.SHL.unidentified }} of {{ q1.coverage.SHL.qualifying }}. Only {{ q1.n_complete }} seasons of the rung 1 + 2 series ({{ q1.complete_first }}–{{ q1.complete_last }}) have every rung-2 league at least 90% identified.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" id="q2">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="close-kicker">Question 2</p>
    <h2 class="slide-q">When did it break?</h2>
    {% set fall = q2.CZE.fall %}
    <p class="slide-a">{% if q2.CZE.sharp %}In <strong>{{ fall.modal.season }}</strong>.{% else %}It did not break in one season: <strong>it wore down</strong>.{% endif %} {% if fall %}The most likely fall is {{ fall.modal.season }}, with {{ pct0(fall.modal.prob) }} probability; the fitted level is now {{ pct0(q2.CZE.fitted.latest_to_peak) }} of its {{ q2.CZE.fitted.peak.season }} peak.{% endif %}</p>
    <figure class="figure-bleed" data-chart="q2-break">
      <table class="fig-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Nation</th><th scope="col">Step</th><th scope="col">Most likely season</th><th scope="col" class="num">Probability</th><th scope="col" class="num">Level after ÷ before (90% interval)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for code in ['CZE'] + q2.compared %}{% for s in q2[code].steps %}
          <tr><td>{{ q2[code].name }}</td><td>{{ 'fall' if s.direction == 'down' else 'rise' }}</td><td>{{ s.modal.season }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct0(s.modal.prob) }}</td><td class="num">{{ times(s.delta_factor.median) }} ({{ f2(s.delta_factor.lo) }}–{{ f2(s.delta_factor.hi) }})</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}{% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <figcaption>How to read it: dots are the players with 20 or more games each season, the line and the band are the model's level and its 90% interval. The bars underneath say how likely each season is to be where a step happened: ink for a fall, pale for a rise. A tall single bar would be a sharp break.{% if fall and q2.CZE.fall_spread %} For Czechia, {{ pct0(q2.CZE.fall_mass_in_spread) }} of the fall's probability is spread over {{ q2.CZE.fall_spread[0] }}–{{ q2.CZE.fall_spread[1] }}, with no season above {{ pct0(fall.modal.prob) }}.{% endif %} Switch to {{ q2[q2.compared[0]].name }} and {{ q2[q2.compared[1]].name }}{% if q2[q2.compared[0]].only_up and q2[q2.compared[1]].only_up %}: both have only rises{% endif %}.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <details class="fold slide-method">
      <summary>How we know</summary>
      <p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">The model</span> A Poisson local-level model, the one the football atlas uses for its series: the log of the expected count follows a random walk plus two step changes, and the step seasons are marginalised over every allowed pair (at least three seasons from the ends and from each other). 2004/05, the lockout, stays in the time index with no likelihood. Priors: σ ~ {{ q2.definitions.priors.sigma }}, step ~ {{ q2.definitions.priors.delta }}.</p>
      {% if fall %}<p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">The Czech fall</span> The step is {{ times(fall.delta_factor.median) }} (90% interval {{ f2(fall.delta_factor.lo) }}–{{ f2(fall.delta_factor.hi) }}); the probability that it lowers the level is {{ f2(fall.p_down) }}. The earlier rise is dated to {{ q2.CZE.ups[0].modal.season if q2.CZE.ups else '–' }}. The fitted level peaked at about {{ q2.CZE.fitted.peak.level|round|int }} players in {{ q2.CZE.fitted.peak.season }} and is {{ q2.CZE.fitted.latest.level|round|int }} in {{ q2.CZE.fitted.latest.season }}.</p>{% endif %}
      <p class="slide-how"><span class="slide-how-label">Diagnostics</span> {{ q2.definitions.sampler.chains }} chains × {{ q2.definitions.sampler.draws }} draws after {{ q2.definitions.sampler.tune }} tuning, seed {{ q2.definitions.sampler.seed }}; largest R-hat {{ '%.3f'|format(q2.max_rhat) }}, {{ q2.divergences }} divergent transition{{ '' if q2.divergences == 1 else 's' }} over the three fits. There is no forecast: the atlas is descriptive.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" id="q3">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="close-kicker">Question 3</p>
    <h2 class="slide-q">Where is it thin?</h2>
    {% set top = q3.top_shortfall %}
    <p class="slide-a">{% if q3.u21_home == 0 %}In the youngest band: <strong>no Czech skater aged 21 or under</strong> reaches the games threshold in the NHL or rung 2 in {{ q3.season }}.{% else %}{{ q3.u21_home }} Czech skaters aged 21 or under reach the threshold in {{ q3.season }}.{% endif %}{% if top %} The largest shortfall is {{ position_word[top.position] }} aged {{ band_word[top.age_band] }}: {{ f1(top.shortfall) }} players below the peer median.{% endif %}</p>
    <figure class="figure-bleed" data-chart="q3-cohorts">
      <table class="fig-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Position, age</th><th scope="col" class="num">Czech players</th><th scope="col" class="num">per million</th><th scope="col" class="num">peer median</th><th scope="col" class="num">short of the median</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for c in q3.cells|sort(attribute='position') %}
          <tr><td>{{ position_word[c.position] }}, {{ c.age_band }}</td><td class="num">{{ c.counts.CZE }}</td><td class="num">{{ f2(c.per_million.CZE) }}</td><td class="num">{{ f2(c.peer_median) }}</td><td class="num">{{ f1(c.shortfall) if c.shortfall > 0 else '–' }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <figcaption>How to read it: one row per position and age band in {{ q3.season }}. The blue dot is Czechia, the ink tick the peer median, the grey dots the peers (hover for names). A hollow dot is a peer left out of that median because more than a quarter of its players have no known age or position: {{ q3.excluded_age|join(' and ') }} in every age band, as the National League and the DEL publish no birth dates. The scale is logarithmic so the small nations stay readable next to Finland and Sweden.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <details class="fold slide-method">
      <summary>How we know</summary>
      <p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">What we did</span> Qualifying players in the NHL and rung 2 in {{ q3.season }}, counted once per person, split by position and by age (season start year minus birth year). The shortfall is the gap to the peer median per million times the Czech population ({{ f1(population_m) }} million): the number of players Czechia would need to reach the median.</p>
      <p class="slide-how"><span class="slide-how-label">Largest shortfalls</span> {% for s in q3.shortfalls %}{{ position_word[s.position] }} {{ s.age_band }}: {{ f1(s.shortfall) }}{{ '; ' if not loop.last else '.' }}{% endfor %}</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" id="q4">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="close-kicker">Question 4</p>
    <h2 class="slide-q">Do young players get ice time at home?</h2>
    <p class="slide-a">{% if q4.home.mean_u21_games_share < q4.peers.Liiga.mean_u21_games_share and q4.home.mean_u21_games_share < q4.peers.SHL.mean_u21_games_share %}Less than in Finland and Sweden.{% else %}About as much as in Finland and Sweden.{% endif %} Under-21 skaters play <strong>{{ pct(q4.home.mean_u21_games_share) }} of Extraliga games</strong> and {{ pct(q4.home.mean_u21_toi_share) }} of its ice time; the Liiga gives them {{ pct(q4.peers.Liiga.mean_u21_games_share) }} and {{ pct(q4.peers.Liiga.mean_u21_toi_share) }}, the SHL {{ pct(q4.peers.SHL.mean_u21_games_share) }} and {{ pct(q4.peers.SHL.mean_u21_toi_share) }}.</p>
    <figure class="figure-bleed" data-chart="q4-youth">
      <table class="fig-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">League</th><th scope="col" class="num">Under-21 share of games</th><th scope="col" class="num">of ice time</th><th scope="col" class="num">Seasons measured</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="is-home"><td>Extraliga</td><td class="num">{{ pct(q4.home.mean_u21_games_share) }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(q4.home.mean_u21_toi_share) }}</td><td class="num">{{ q4.home.measured_seasons }}</td></tr>
          {% for name, s in q4.peers.items() %}<tr><td>{{ name }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(s.mean_u21_games_share) }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(s.mean_u21_toi_share) }}</td><td class="num">{{ s.measured_seasons }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <figcaption>How to read it: the share of all skater games (or of skater ice time) played by skaters aged 20 or less, season by season over {{ q4.window }}. The Extraliga is blue, the Liiga ink, the SHL grey. The National League and the DEL are dashed and marked "not measured": they publish no birth dates, so ages are known for only about {{ pct0(q4.unmeasured_known.NL) }} and {{ pct0(q4.unmeasured_known.DEL) }} of their games, and their shares only count the young players who could be linked to another league.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <details class="fold slide-method">
      <summary>How we know</summary>
      <p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">What we did</span> Every skater of every nationality, regular season. A league-season counts as measured when ages are known for at least 90% of its skater games; the Extraliga, Liiga and SHL are measured in all {{ q4.n_seasons }} seasons. Ice time is published by the Extraliga from 2013/14, the Liiga from 2014/15 and the SHL from 2009/10. Goalkeepers are in <a href="#q7">question 7</a>.</p>
      <p class="slide-how"><span class="slide-how-label">Ratios</span> The Extraliga's under-21 share of games is {{ f2(q4.comparison.Liiga.games_share_ratio_home_to_league) }} times the Liiga's and {{ f2(q4.comparison.SHL.games_share_ratio_home_to_league) }} times the SHL's; of ice time, {{ f2(q4.comparison.Liiga.toi_share_ratio_home_to_league) }} and {{ f2(q4.comparison.SHL.toi_share_ratio_home_to_league) }}. In {{ q4.latest_season }} the Extraliga share was {{ pct(q4.home.latest.u21_games_share) }} of games and {{ pct(q4.home.latest.u21_toi_share) }} of ice time.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" id="q5">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="close-kicker">Question 5</p>
    <h2 class="slide-q">How do they fare abroad?</h2>
    {% set n = q5.home.NHL %}
    <p class="slide-a">In the NHL, Czech skaters play <strong>{{ f2(n.median_toi_ratio) }} times</strong> the median ice time of their position and score {{ f2(n.median_ppg_ratio) }} times its points per game. In the Liiga ({{ f2(q5.home.Liiga.median_toi_ratio) }}, {{ f2(q5.home.Liiga.median_ppg_ratio) }}) and the SHL ({{ f2(q5.home.SHL.median_toi_ratio) }}, {{ f2(q5.home.SHL.median_ppg_ratio) }}){% if q5.words.Liiga == ('above', 'above') and q5.words.SHL == ('above', 'above') %} they are above the median on both counts{% else %} the ratios are as shown{% endif %}.</p>
    <figure class="figure-bleed" data-chart="q5-abroad">
      <table class="fig-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">League</th><th scope="col" class="num">Czech players</th><th scope="col" class="num">player-seasons</th><th scope="col" class="num">ice time ÷ median</th><th scope="col" class="num">points per game ÷ median</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for lg, v in q5.home.items() %}<tr><td>{{ lg }}</td><td class="num">{{ v.players }}</td><td class="num">{{ v.player_seasons }}</td><td class="num">{{ f2(v.median_toi_ratio) }}</td><td class="num">{{ f2(v.median_ppg_ratio) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table>
      <figcaption>How to read it: each dot is a nation's median skater in a league over {{ q5.window }}, as a multiple of the league-season median at the same position (1.0 = the median). Czechia is the blue dot; filled ink dots are peers with ten or more player-seasons in that league, hollow ones fewer. Switch between ice time and points per game. {% if q5.own_below_one %}A league's own players (Finns in the Liiga, Swedes in the SHL) sit below 1.0: they make up most of the roster, depth included, and the imported players are compared with them.{% endif %}</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <details class="fold slide-method">
      <summary>How we know</summary>
      <p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">What we did</span> Qualifying skaters (the games threshold) over {{ q5.window }}; each player-season is divided by the median of all qualifying skaters of the same league, season and position (forward or defenceman), and the table shows the median of those ratios. {{ q5.n_player_seasons }} Czech player-seasons in all; {{ q5.unknown_position }} have no position and are left out.</p>
      <p class="slide-how"><span class="slide-how-label">By position</span> NHL forwards {{ f2(q5.by_position.NHL.F.median_toi_ratio) }} (ice time) and {{ f2(q5.by_position.NHL.F.median_ppg_ratio) }} (points), NHL defencemen {{ f2(q5.by_position.NHL.D.median_toi_ratio) }} and {{ f2(q5.by_position.NHL.D.median_ppg_ratio) }}; Liiga forwards {{ f2(q5.by_position.Liiga.F.median_ppg_ratio) }} on points, SHL forwards {{ f2(q5.by_position.SHL.F.median_ppg_ratio) }}.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" id="q6">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="close-kicker">Question 6</p>
    <h2 class="slide-q">What is the national team built from?</h2>
    <p class="slide-a">Since {{ q6.first_year }}, Czech World Championship and Olympic rosters have been on average <strong>{{ pct0(q6.home['1']) }} NHL</strong>, {{ pct0(q6.home['home']) }} Extraliga, {{ pct0(q6.home.khl) }} KHL and {{ pct0(q6.home['2']) }} rung 2.</p>
    <figure class="figure-bleed" data-chart="q6-roster">
      <table class="fig-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Tournament</th><th scope="col" class="num">NHL</th><th scope="col" class="num">rung 2</th><th scope="col" class="num">Extraliga</th><th scope="col" class="num">KHL</th><th scope="col" class="num">other</th><th scope="col" class="num">players</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for e in q6.events %}<tr{% if e is sameas q6.last_event %} class="is-home"{% endif %}><td>{{ 'Olympics' if e.event == 'OG' else 'World Championship' }} {{ e.year }}</td><td class="num">{{ e['1'] }}</td><td class="num">{{ e['2'] }}</td><td class="num">{{ e.home }}</td><td class="num">{{ e.khl }}</td><td class="num">{{ e.other + e.unknown }}</td><td class="num">{{ e.players }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table>
      <figcaption>How to read it: each bar is a nation's roster spots by the league the player's club was in at the time of the tournament, averaged over the {{ q6.n_events }} World Championships and Olympics since {{ q6.first_year }}: NHL in blue, rung 2 in ink, the Extraliga pale, the KHL hatched, other leagues grey. The second view is Czechia tournament by tournament{% if q6.last_khl_event and q6.last_khl_event is not sameas q6.last_event %}: no KHL player has been on the Czech roster since the {{ 'Olympics' if q6.last_khl_event.event == 'OG' else 'World Championship' }} {{ q6.last_khl_event.year }}{% endif %}; at the {{ q6.last_label }} the roster had {{ q6.last_event['1'] }} NHL players, {{ q6.last_event['2'] }} from rung 2 and {{ q6.last_event.home }} from the Extraliga.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <details class="fold slide-method">
      <summary>How we know</summary>
      <p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">What we did</span> Rosters from the English Wikipedia articles for each World Championship and Olympic tournament since {{ q6.first_year }} (CC BY-SA 4.0), each player linked to his league records. A player's club is placed in a league by these rules in order: the league Wikipedia gives, a list of KHL clubs, his NHL career record for that season, his own league row, a team-name match, then the club's country.</p>
      <p class="slide-how"><span class="slide-how-label">Placement</span> {% for k, v in q6.basis_counts.items() %}{{ k|replace('_', ' ') }} {{ num(v) }}{{ ', ' if not loop.last else '' }}{% endfor %} roster rows (all nations). The Czech NHL share ranks {{ ordinal(q6.nhl_rank) }} of the ten nations.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" id="q7">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="close-kicker">Question 7</p>
    <h2 class="slide-q">Goalkeepers</h2>
    <p class="slide-a">{{ q7.home.nhl }} Czech goalkeepers reached the threshold in the NHL in {{ q7.season }} and {{ q7.home.top5 }} in the NHL plus rung 2: <strong>{{ f2(q7.home.top5_per_million) }} per million</strong>, {{ ordinal(q7.home.rank_top5) }} of {{ q7.n_nations }}, against a peer median of {{ f2(q7.peer_median.top5_per_million) }}.</p>
    <figure class="figure-bleed" data-chart="q7-bars">
      {{ nation_table(q7.table, 'nhl', 'nhl_per_million', 'NHL goalkeepers') }}
      <figcaption>How to read it: as in question 1, for goalkeepers with at least the pro-rated games threshold in {{ q7.season }}. Czechia is {{ ordinal(q7.rank_nhl) }} in the NHL at {{ f2(q7.home.nhl_per_million) }} per million (peer median {{ f2(q7.peer_median.nhl_per_million) }}).</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="figure-bleed" data-chart="q7-series">
      <table class="fig-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Season</th><th scope="col" class="num">Czech NHL goalkeepers</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for s, n in q7.home_series %}<tr><td>{{ s }}</td><td class="num">{{ n if n is not none else 'lockout' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table>
      <figcaption>How to read it: qualifying NHL goalkeepers per nation, season by season. The Czech count is {{ q7.series_latest }} in {{ q7.season }}{% if q7.series_is_max %}, as many as in any season since 1995/96{% else %}; the most was {{ q7.series_max }}{% endif %}.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <details class="fold slide-method">
      <summary>How we know</summary>
      <p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">Abroad</span> Czech goalkeepers' save percentage against the league-season median, {{ q7.window_abroad }}: NHL {{ '%+.1f'|format(q7.abroad.NHL.median_save_pct_minus_median * 100) }} points ({{ q7.abroad.NHL.goalies }} goalkeepers), Liiga {{ '%+.1f'|format(q7.abroad.Liiga.median_save_pct_minus_median * 100) }} ({{ q7.abroad.Liiga.goalies }}), SHL {{ '%+.1f'|format(q7.abroad.SHL.median_save_pct_minus_median * 100) }} ({{ q7.abroad.SHL.goalies }}). Small numbers: read them as descriptive.</p>
      <p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">Young goalkeepers at home</span> Goalkeepers aged 23 or less play {{ pct(q7.youth.Extraliga) }} of Extraliga goalkeeper games, against {{ pct(q7.youth.Liiga) }} in the Liiga and {{ pct(q7.youth.SHL) }} in the SHL ({{ q4.window }}). Czech goalkeepers played {{ pct0(q7.extraliga_home_share) }} of Extraliga goalkeeper games in {{ q7.season }}.</p>
      <p class="slide-how"><span class="slide-how-label">National team</span> Of {{ q7.nt.roster_spots }} goalkeeper roster spots since 2010, {{ q7.nt.by_category['1'] }} went to NHL goalkeepers, {{ q7.nt.by_category.khl }} to KHL goalkeepers, {{ q7.nt.by_category.home }} to Extraliga goalkeepers and {{ q7.nt.by_category['2'] }} to rung 2.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

{# This autumn: dated news (config/news/cze.yaml) beside the atlas's own numbers; only confirmed,
   footnoted facts. Left out when there is no news file. #}
{% macro fn(ns) %}<sup class="fn">{% for n in ns %}{% if not loop.first %},{% endif %}<a href="#autumn-src-{{ n }}">{{ n }}</a>{% endfor %}</sup>{% endmacro %}
{% if autumn %}
{% set au = autumn %}
{% set cp = au.captain %}
{% set co = au.coach %}
<section class="slide autumn" id="autumn">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="close-kicker">News</p>
    <h2 class="slide-q">This autumn</h2>
    <p class="autumn-asof">Atlas data as of {{ au.data_as_of }}; news as of {{ au.news_as_of }}</p>
    <div class="autumn-body">
      <p class="autumn-lede">Two dated items of news, with their sources listed at the end of this section. The numbers beside them are the atlas's own, from its snapshot, which this section does not refresh.</p>

      <h3>A new head coach of the national team</h3>
      <p>{{ co.new }} succeeds {{ co.previous }} as head coach of the Czech men's national team. {{ co.approved_by[0]|upper }}{{ co.approved_by[1:] }} approved the appointment on {{ co.approved }}, with {{ co.contract_years }}-year contracts.{{ fn(co.notes_approved) }} The staff: {{ co.new }} with coaches {{ co.coaches|join(' and ') }}, goalkeeping coach {{ co.goalkeeping_coach }}, and {{ co.general_manager }} as general manager in place of {{ co.previous_general_manager }}.{{ fn(co.notes_staff) }} The first game under the new staff is on {{ co.first_game.date }} against {{ co.first_game.opponent }} at the {{ co.first_game.venue }} ({{ co.first_game.competition }}).{{ fn(co.first_game.notes) }}</p>
      <p class="capita-note">What the national team's rosters have been built from since {{ q6.first_year }}, by league: <a href="#q6">question 6</a>.</p>

      <h3>A club captaincy in the NHL</h3>
      <p>On {{ cp.named }} the {{ cp.club }} named {{ cp.name }} the {{ cp.nth }} captain in the club's history.{{ fn(cp.notes_named) }} The previous captain was {{ cp.previous }} ({{ cp.previous_note }}).{{ fn(cp.notes_previous) }} According to hokej.cz, {{ cp.name.split(' ')[-1] }} is the {{ cp.czech_nth }} Czech to be a permanent captain in the NHL.{{ fn(cp.notes_czech_nth) }} The captaincy is with his NHL club, not a national-team role.</p>
      {% set s = cp.season %}
      {% set a = cp.abroad %}
      <dl class="autumn-stats" aria-label="{{ cp.name }}, {{ s.league }} {{ s.season }}, from the atlas">
        <div><dt>{{ s.league }} games, {{ s.season }}</dt><dd>{{ num(s.games) }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Points</dt><dd>{{ num(s.points) }} <span class="muted">{{ num(s.goals) }} goals, {{ num(s.assists) }} assists</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Ice time per game</dt><dd>{{ mmss(s.toi_per_game_s) }}{% if a %} <span class="muted">median {{ mmss(a.median_toi_per_game_s) }}</span>{% endif %}</dd></div>
        {% if a %}
        <div><dt>Points per game</dt><dd>{{ f2(a.points_per_game) }} <span class="muted">median {{ f2(a.median_points_per_game) }}</span></dd></div>
        {% endif %}
      </dl>
      <p class="capita-note">From the atlas's pool data, {{ s.league }} {{ s.season }}. The median is over all {{ s.league }} {{ cp.position_word }} who reached the games threshold that season, as in <a href="#q5">question 5</a>. His seasons since {{ pool.window.split('–')[0] }} are on the <a href="atlas/">pool page</a>.</p>

      <h3 class="autumn-sources-h">Sources</h3>
      <ol class="autumn-sources">
        {% for src in au.sources %}
        <li id="autumn-src-{{ src.n }}">{{ src.publisher }} ({{ src.date or 'n.d.' }}). <a href="{{ src.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ src.url }}</a>, accessed {{ src.accessed }}.</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section class="methodology" id="methodology">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>How it is built, and where it stops</h2>

    <h3 id="data-sources">Sources</h3>
    <table class="sources-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">What</th><th scope="col">Fields used</th><th scope="col">Accessed</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for s in sources %}
        <tr><td><a href="{{ s.url }}">{{ s.name }}</a></td><td>{{ s.what }}</td><td>{{ s.fields }}</td><td class="mono">{{ s.accessed }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Only public statistics are used: names, birth dates, nationality and season statistics. Every source was fetched once, with at least a second between requests and within its robots.txt, into a raw cache; the processed tables are committed in <code>data/snapshot/</code> with a SHA-256 list, so a clean clone rebuilds every number here without fetching. The NHL's terms allow non-commercial informational use; this is a non-commercial page that cites its sources. Wikipedia rosters are used under CC BY-SA 4.0, each page at the revision listed in <code>data/snapshot/rosters_sources.json</code>.</p>

    <h3 id="linking">Linking players across leagues</h3>
    <p>{{ num(linking.persons) }} people in all, {{ num(linking.with_nat) }} of them with a nationality. Records are matched in four steps: folded name plus full birth date; first initial, surname and birth date (for Dan and Daniel); for records without a birth date, the name alone when exactly one person of that name played within four seasons and his birth year does not contradict it; and finally records still unmatched are joined within the same league on the same name.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="linking-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">League</th><th scope="col" class="num">Records</th><th scope="col" class="num">With birth date</th><th scope="col" class="num">Linked on name + birth date</th><th scope="col" class="num">Linked on name only</th><th scope="col" class="num">Ambiguous</th><th scope="col" class="num">Unmatched</th><th scope="col" class="num">Joined within league</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for r in linking.rows %}
        <tr><td>{{ r.league }}</td><td class="num">{{ num(r.records) }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct0(r.with_birth_date_share) }}</td><td class="num">{{ num(r.linked_on_name_and_birth_date_to_another_source) }}</td><td class="num">{{ num(r.name_only_linked) if r.without_birth_date else '–' }}</td><td class="num">{{ num(r.ambiguous) if r.without_birth_date else '–' }}</td><td class="num">{{ num(r.unmatched) if r.without_birth_date else '–' }}</td><td class="num">{{ num(r.joined_within_league_on_name) if r.without_birth_date else '–' }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <p>"Unmatched" records keep the nationality their own league gives them, which for the DEL before 2022/23 and for foreign licences in the National League is none. {{ linking.conflicts.persons }} people carry conflicting nationality codes; in {{ linking.conflicts.czech_eligibility_overridden_by_citizenship }} of them an Extraliga "Czech" (the foreigner flag) is overridden by a citizenship or national-team code. {{ linking.swapped|length }} Wikipedia roster birth dates matched no league record until day and month were swapped or moved by one day; they are corrected in the analysis and listed in <code>outputs/linking.json</code>.</p>

    <h3 id="definitions">Definitions</h3>
    <dl class="defs">
      <dt>Games threshold</dt><dd>{{ q1.threshold_def }}. The headline also reports any game and a flat 20.</dd>
      <dt>Age</dt><dd>Season start year minus birth year; under 21 means 20 or less.</dd>
      <dt>Population</dt><dd>Eurostat <code>demo_gind</code>, 1 January of the season's second year.</dd>
      <dt>Complete season</dt><dd>A rung 1 + 2 season counts as complete when every rung-2 league has at least 90% of its qualifying players' nationality identified.</dd>
      <dt>Season</dt><dd>Regular season only, every league.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h3 id="reproducibility">Reproducibility</h3>
    <p><code>make restore-snapshot</code> puts the committed snapshot in place, <code>make verify-snapshot</code> checks its hashes, <code>make analysis</code> recomputes <code>outputs/</code> (about six minutes, mostly the break model) and <code>make pages</code> renders this page and the pool page from them. Each output file records the SHA-256 of the snapshot files it was built from, and the tests fail when the snapshot changes without the outputs being rebuilt. Every number in this text is read from <code>outputs/</code> at render time.</p>

    <h3 id="limitations">Limitations</h3>
    <ul class="nx-limits">
      <li><strong>KHL</strong> Excluded by design. It is where {{ pct0(q6.home.khl) }} of Czech national-team roster spots since 2010 came from, so the pool counted here is smaller than the pool the national team drew on, most of all before 2014 and before 2022.</li>
      <li><strong>AHL</strong> Not fetched (terms). An AHL season appears only when the player also has an NHL career record, which favours those who made it.</li>
      <li><strong>Birth dates</strong> The National League and the DEL publish none, so their players' ages come only from a link to another league. That removes {{ q3.excluded_age|join(' and ') }} from the age medians in question 3 and leaves the NL and DEL youth shares in question 4 unmeasured.</li>
      <li><strong>Nationality</strong> For {{ pool.eligibility_only }} of the {{ pool.players }} Czech players on the pool page, the only evidence is the Extraliga foreigner flag or a licence, which is eligibility, not citizenship. The DEL published no nationality before 2022/23, so the rung 1 + 2 series before {{ q1.complete_first }} is a lower bound.</li>
      <li><strong>Name-only links</strong> Records without a birth date are linked on the name alone, only when one candidate exists within four seasons; ambiguous and unmatched counts are in the table above.</li>
      <li><strong>Population</strong> A per-million rate compares nations of very different sizes; a handful of players moves a small nation's rate a lot.</li>
      <li><strong>Descriptive only</strong> Nothing here predicts a season, rates a player beyond his published statistics or advises selection.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="changes">Change log</h3>
    <ul class="changelog">
      <li><span class="mono">2026-09-29</span> A <a href="#autumn">This autumn</a> section: two dated, sourced items of news (the national team's new head coach and staff; David Pastrňák's club captaincy in Boston), beside the atlas's own numbers.</li>
      <li><span class="mono">2026-09-29</span> Rebuilt on the football atlas's model: ten nations, a two-rung league ladder, fetchers with a committed snapshot, one analysis module per question, interactive charts drawn from <code>outputs/</code>, and a <a href="atlas/">pool page</a>. The style map, the AI layer and the video proof of concept of the earlier version are withdrawn.</li>
      <li><span class="mono">2026-09-22</span> The site became English only.</li>
      <li><span class="mono">2026-05-18</span> First version: a style map of Czech players from a crosswalk of league statistics.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="close" id="close">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="close-kicker">What this is for</p>
    <p class="close-statement">The same measured questions, asked every summer and answered the same way, with the uncertainty on the page — and a name behind every number.</p>
    <p class="close-links"><a href="atlas/">Every Czech player in the pool</a> · <a href="#take">What to take from it</a> · <a href="#limitations">Limitations</a> · <a href="https://football.bsandova.com/">The football atlas</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
